From 89866962d11c8de4d1e3b3f3c54050904658bb1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:48:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add self-service dealer onboarding document upload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires up the "Application form coming soon" button on Store.jsx (which
did nothing — no onClick at all) to a new /dealer/apply screen where a
pending dealer can submit their own onboarding documents instead of an
admin having to enter everything by hand.

New dealer-facing flow (DealerApply.jsx):
- Registration type toggle (Unregistered/Registered) + GSTIN field.
- Identity documents (Aadhaar, PAN, and GST certificate when registered)
  via plain file upload, stored in a new private "dealer-documents"
  bucket — viewed only through short-lived signed URLs, never a public
  link, since these are sensitive documents.
- Owner photo, staff photo, shop outside photo, shop board photo, a 5s
  shop-interior video, and a 15s intro video — all captured live via the
  existing CameraPhotoSlot/CameraVideoSlot components (already proven in
  the field-rep check-in flow), so there's no gallery-upload path for a
  fake/old photo. CameraVideoSlot's previously-hardcoded 5s cap is now a
  `maxSeconds` prop (default still 5) so the 15s intro video can reuse it
  without touching the existing DayCheckIn behavior.
- Submits via a new submit_dealer_application() RPC that re-validates
  completeness server-side and flips dealer_application_status to
  'under_review' (the existing banner for that state already exists in
  Store.jsx, unchanged).
- A new "rejected" banner + Reapply button, and a Profile.jsx shortcut,
  since a rejected dealer previously had no path back into the app to
  fix and resubmit anything.

Admin side (per Sumaksh's picks: review surfaces in both screens, and
Approve is allowed through a warning rather than hard-blocked):
- AdminDealers.jsx: new "Identity Documents" tiles (signed-URL view,
  admin can still upload/replace as a fallback) alongside the existing
  Photos & Media grid, which now also shows the two new fields (Shop
  Outside, Intro Video). Approve asks for confirmation first if the
  application is missing anything.
- DealerCRM.jsx: read-only "Documents & Photos" summary in the Overview
  tab (view-only — replacing a file still goes through AdminDealers.jsx
  to keep upload logic in one place) with the same Approve warning gate.

Schema (supabase/migrations/dealer_onboarding_documents.sql): new
profiles columns (doc_aadhaar, doc_pan, doc_gst_cert, shop_outside_photo,
intro_video, documents_submitted_at); a new private "dealer-documents"
storage bucket + RLS (owner or admin only, unlike the existing public
dealer-media/staff-media buckets); a dealer-can-write-own-folder policy
added to the existing "dealer-media" bucket (previously admin-only);
update_my_dealer_field() — a narrow, whitelisted self-service RPC
(mirrors update_my_photo()'s defense-in-depth reasoning: no blanket
"dealer can edit own row" policy, and blocked once already approved);
and submit_dealer_application() for the completeness check + status
flip.

Reuses the existing owner_photo/staff1_photo/shop_board_photo/shop_video
columns (already admin-writable) rather than adding parallel ones, so
whatever a dealer uploads themselves shows up automatically in the
admin screens that already read those columns.

